"Interlacing Property of a Family of Generating Polynomials over Dyck Paths | The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics (https://www.combinatorics.org/ojs/index.php/eljc/article/view/v31i1p63)\nciteturn9search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.6 years ago; Crawled: last month; # Interlacing Property of a Family of Generating Polynomials over Dyck Paths ... 2024-03-22 ... Wang, B., & Zhang, C.\n\n# Interlacing Property of a Family of Generating Polynomials over Dyck Paths\n\n  * Bo Wang\n  * Candice X.T. Zhang\n\nDOI: https://doi.org/10.37236/12375\n\n### Abstract\n\nIn the study of a tantalizing symmetry on Catalan objects, Bóna et al. introduced a family of polynomials $\\{W_{n,k}(x)\\}_{n\\geq k\\geq 0}$ defined by\n$$\nW_{n,k}(x)=\\sum_{m=0}^{k}w_{n,k,m}x^{m},\n$$\nwhere $w_{n,k,m}$ counts the number of Dyck paths of semilength $n$ with $k$ occurrences of $UD$ and $m$ occurrences of $UUD$. They proposed two conjectures on the interlacing property of these polynomials, one of which states that $\\{W_{n,k}(x)\\}_{n\\geq k}$ is a Sturm sequence for any fixed $k\\geq 1$, and the other states that $\\{W_{n,k}(x)\\}_{1\\leq k\\leq n}$ is a Sturm-unimodal sequence for any fixed $n\\geq 1$. In this paper, we obtain certain recurrence relations for $W_{n,k}(x)$, and further confirm their conjectures.\n\nPublished\n\n2024-03-22\n\nHow to Cite\n\nWang, B., & Zhang, C. X. (2024). Interlacing Property of a Family of Generating Polynomials over Dyck Paths. The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, 31(1), #P1.63. https://doi.org/10.37236/12375\n\nIssue\n\nVolume 31, Issue 1 (2024)\n\nArticle Number\n\nP1.63--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndblp: Interlacing Property of a Family of Generating Polynomials over Dyck Paths. (https://dblp.dagstuhl.de/rec/journals/combinatorics/WangZ24.html)\nciteturn9search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # \"Interlacing Property of a Family of Generating Polynomials over Dyck Paths.\" ... Bo Wang